# Career141 TA Platform — stage one, model access only.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and paste ONE key in. Nothing else in the app
# needs a credential yet: the Convex connection is a later step, and every
# feature below still works without a key — it falls back to the deterministic
# output and says on screen that it did.
#
# .env.local is gitignored. Do not paste a key into chat, into this example
# file, or into any file that is tracked.

# Models. The desk runs on OpenRouter (one key, every model); the direct keys
# are the fallback. If OpenRouter is set it is used for writing and reading.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Web search for Suggestions, Benchmark and Research (21 Sep).
#   searxng — a SearXNG instance: no key, no bill (needs SEARXNG_URL)
#   serper  — Google through serper.dev (needs SERPER_API_KEY)
#   openai  — OpenAI's own web search (needs OPENAI_API_KEY)
# Unset: SearXNG when SEARXNG_URL is set, otherwise Serper when its key is
# there, otherwise nothing searches. OpenAI is never picked by itself — every
# server has an OpenAI key for other work, and falling back to it turned a
# missing Serper key into paid searches nobody asked for (21 Sep). To run the
# desk on OpenAI web search, say so here.
SERPER_API_KEY=
C141_SEARCH_PROVIDER=
# SearXNG instances, in the order they are asked. A public instance rate-limits
# and may serve JSON not at all (403) — Research fires about thirty searches
# per opening — so name several and the next one answers when one refuses.
# One self-hosted instance is the plan; then this is a single address.
SEARXNG_URL=
# Which engines to ask, comma-separated. Unset: google,bing,yahoo. Google alone
# stopped Research on 24 Sep when Google sent the server a CAPTCHA and there
# was nothing else to ask. Leave out Brave, DuckDuckGo, Qwant and Google CSE:
# measured 23 Sep, they refuse or time out from the server, and waiting for
# them cost six seconds on every search.
SEARXNG_ENGINES=
# How hard SearXNG may be asked. Unset: two searches at once, 700ms apart.
# Eighteen at once — what Research reaches — made Google CAPTCHA on the server
# and suspend itself for everybody (23 Sep). Raise only with evidence.
SEARXNG_CONCURRENCY=
SEARXNG_MIN_GAP_MS=
# Which model runs those searches. Unset: gpt-4.1-mini.
C141_MODEL_SEARCH_OPENAI=
# Who researches the client: openai | openrouter | anthropic. Unset: OpenRouter.
C141_RESEARCH_PROVIDER=

# Optional. Leave as-is unless you want a specific model.
C141_MODEL=

# Turns on grounded Research (company facts with sources). Without it, Research
# reports what it cannot verify rather than inventing company details.
C141_WEB_SEARCH=on

# Admin keys for log streaming (npm run convex:logs:prod / convex:logs:staging).
# Find these in the team 1Password vault — never paste them here or in code.
CONVEX_PROD_ADMIN_KEY=
CONVEX_STAGING_ADMIN_KEY=

# The owner's Claude subscription for research and suggestions (24 Sep).
# Make the token with `claude setup-token` on your own machine — it is a
# password; keep it out of git and chat. Tasks allowed: plan (Research and
# Suggestions), research, jd. CV/candidate tasks are refused whatever is set.
# Anything the subscription cannot answer falls back to OpenRouter.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
C141_CLAUDE_SUB_TASKS=

# Claude for Research and Benchmark through the company's Anthropic API key
# (24 Sep) — the sanctioned route for an app; the subscription above is one
# person's login and Anthropic's terms do not allow it for the whole desk.
# Uses ANTHROPIC_API_KEY above. Set C141_CLAUDE_API_TASKS=plan to turn it on.
# Same tasks allowed as the subscription; CV/candidate tasks are refused.
# Model: claude-opus-5 unless C141_CLAUDE_API_MODEL says otherwise.
# Anything Claude cannot answer falls back to OpenRouter.
C141_CLAUDE_API_TASKS=
C141_CLAUDE_API_MODEL=
